# `node-monorepo-demo`

Short Node.js monorepo / multi-module demo that follows the lifecycle mapping from `temp.md`.

### Modules

- `@demo/module-a` - base module `a`
- `@demo/module-b` - base module `b`
- `@demo/module-c` - depends on `a` and `b`
- `@demo/module-d` - depends on `c`

### Build output

Each module build creates both outputs under `packages/<module>/dist`:

- `index.js` - non-minified artifact
- `index.min.js` - minified artifact with legal comments preserved

Package tarballs are created under `.artifacts`, and deployment descriptors are prepared under `.deploy`.

### Scripts

Use Node from `C:\pub\node-v24.15.0-win-x64`.

Run the lifecycle from the repository root in this order:

```powershell
$env:Path = 'C:\pub\node-v24.15.0-win-x64;' + $env:Path
npm ci
npm run clean
npm run validate
npm run format
npm run lint
npm run build
npm test
npm run pre-integration-test
npm run integration-test
npm run post-integration-test
npm run pre-e2e-test
npm run e2e-test
npm run post-e2e-test
npm run coverage
npm run security
npm run verify
npm run package
npm run sbom
npm run sign
npm run install-local
npm run publish
npm run deploy
```

### Build one module

Example for module `a` only:

```powershell
$env:Path = 'C:\pub\node-v24.15.0-win-x64;' + $env:Path
Set-Location .\packages\a
npm run validate
npm run build
npm test
npm run integration-test
npm run e2e-test
```
